Schedule Deferred User Tasks

Sometimes you need to run one or more commands at a specific future time. Schedule commands are called tasks or jobs and the deferred terms indicates that these tasks run in furture

one available solution to RHEL users to schedule deferred tasks is at command, which is installed and enabled by default

at package provides the atd system deamon, and the at and atq commands to interact with deamon

sytax: at timespec command

-----------------------

inspect and managed deferred user jobs

to list the pending jobs for the current user, use the atq or at -l command

>atq
>at -l

install at : dnf install -y at

start the at deamon in server
systemctl start at

systemctl is-active atd


[root@ip-172-31-7-169 ec2-user]# at 17:47
warning: commands will be executed using /bin/sh
at Sun Nov  1 17:47:00 2026
at> echo "time is 5:47 Pm IST"
at> <EOT>   #press ctrl+D to save the job and exit

job 1 at Sun Nov  1 17:47:00 2026

atq

it will giv job id, time and user

at -c job_id

it will give whole contents of the job including main commands + env variables at the time of scheduling this command
